4.5 Order creation

When a customer confirms an order:

1. Validate all fields on the server.
2. Load the product and its current price from MySQL.
3. Check stock and availability.
4. Validate the fulfilment method.
5. Validate delivery settings and applicable charges.
6. Recalculate the subtotal and final total on the server.
7. Begin a database transaction.
8. Lock or safely recheck the relevant stock records.
9. Create the order and order-item snapshot.
10. Update stock atomically if the business uses stock deduction at order placement.
11. Commit the transaction.
12. Display the confirmation page.

If any operation fails, roll back the transaction and display an appropriate message.

Prevent duplicate orders caused by double-clicking, retries, or refreshing the confirmation page. Use a suitable server-side idempotency mechanism or equivalent reliable approach.

Make the stock-deduction policy explicit and consistent with the order-cancellation policy.

